    pm:nameForm "thet-em-aua" ;
    pm:nameRole "one of the eight planks in the hull of the boat of chapter 99" ;
    skos:definition "One of the eight names answered together when the planks in the hull say tell us our names. The eight are given in one breath and in one order: Mesthi, Hapi, Tuamautef, Qebh-sennuf, Haqau, Thet-em-Aua, Maa-an-tef, Ari-nef-tchesef. The first four are the sons of Horus, who are named elsewhere in the corpus; the last four are named here and, so far as this run could find, nowhere else in it."@en ;
    skos:note "Budge glosses the name: he who seizeth by violence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:EgyptianRitual ;
    dcterms:source "Book of the Dead, chapter 99, the names of the parts of the boat, Papyrus of Nu (British Museum No. 10,477, sheets 21 and 22), in the English of E. A. Wallis Budge, London: Kegan Paul, Trench, Trübner, 1901, vol. II, pp. 299-300" .

pmc:AegyptiaMaaAnTef a pm:Naming ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BookOfTheDead ;
    rdfs:label "Maa-an-tef"@en, "Maa-an-tef"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "maa-an-tef" ;
    pm:nameRole "one of the eight planks in the hull of the boat of chapter 99" ;
    skos:definition "One of the eight names answered together when the planks in the hull say tell us our names. The eight are given in one breath and in one order: Mesthi, Hapi, Tuamautef, Qebh-sennuf, Haqau, Thet-em-Aua, Maa-an-tef, Ari-nef-tchesef. The first four are the sons of Horus, who are named elsewhere in the corpus; the last four are named here and, so far as this run could find, nowhere else in it."@en ;
    skos:note "Budge glosses the name: he who seeth what the father bringeth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:EgyptianRitual ;
    dcterms:source "Book of the Dead, chapter 99, the names of the parts of the boat, Papyrus of Nu (British Museum No. 10,477, sheets 21 and 22), in the English of E. A. Wallis Budge, London: Kegan Paul, Trench, Trübner, 1901, vol. II, pp. 299-300" .

pmc:AegyptiaAriNefTchesef a pm:Naming ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BookOfTheDead ;
    rdfs:label "Ari-nef-tchesef"@en, "Ari-nef-tchesef"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "ari-nef-tchesef" ;
    pm:nameRole "one of the eight planks in the hull of the boat of chapter 99" ;
    skos:definition "One of the eight names answered together when the planks in the hull say tell us our names. The eight are given in one breath and in one order: Mesthi, Hapi, Tuamautef, Qebh-sennuf, Haqau, Thet-em-Aua, Maa-an-tef, Ari-nef-tchesef. The first four are the sons of Horus, who are named elsewhere in the corpus; the last four are named here and, so far as this run could find, nowhere else in it."@en ;
    skos:note "Budge glosses the name in the chapter: he who made himself. His vocabulary to the same recension carries the headword separately and gives it a different sense — name of a plank or peg in the magical boat — so the volume that elsewhere identifies a bearer here identifies a piece of timber. The two readings are recorded side by side and neither is preferred."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:EgyptianRitual ;
    dcterms:source "Book of the Dead, chapter 99, the names of the parts of the boat, Papyrus of Nu (British Museum No. 10,477, sheets 21 and 22), in the English of E. A. Wallis Budge, London: Kegan Paul, Trench, Trübner, 1901, vol. II, pp. 299-300" ,
        "Budge, A Hieroglyphic Vocabulary to the Theban Recension of the Book of the Dead, London: Kegan Paul, 1911, s.v. Ari-nef-tchesef" .
